quake series off Hualien, M7.3. The east-coast rail line cut.","date":"1951-10-22"},{"t":27,"mag":7.3,"name":"Kern County","pos":[35.0,-119.0],"dl":"BAKERSFIELD","line":"Kern County earthquake, M7.3. Tehachapi in ruins; the Southern Pacific tunnels collapsed.","date":"1952-07-21"},{"t":28,"mag":9.0,"name":"Kamchatka","pos":[52.75,159.5],"dl":"PETROPAVLOVSK","line":"Kamchatka earthquake, M9.0. Tsunami across the Pacific; Hilo flooded again. Severo-Kurilsk erased — Moscow does not report it.","date":"1952-11-04"},{"t":29,"mag":7.3,"name":"Yenice–Gönen","pos":[40.0,27.3],"dl":"ISTANBUL","line":"Yenice–Gönen earthquake, M7.3, south of the Marmara.","date":"1953-03-18"},{"t":35,"mag":6.7,"name":"Orléansville","pos":[36.3,1.5],"dl":"ALGIERS","line":"Orléansville earthquake, M6.7. 1,250 dead in the Chélif valley.","date":"1954-09-09"}],"weather":[{"t":3,"dur":3,"region":"Black Sea Steppe","kind":"drought","dl":"KIEV","line":"Drought across the Ukraine and Moldavia. The harvest fails; Moscow keeps exporting grain.","unmade":"The drought the Ukraine expected did not come. The harvest holds. Moscow exports anyway.","worse":"Drought across the Ukraine, worse than any on record. The villages stop reporting.","date":"1946-07"},{"t":5,"dur":1,"region":"North Sea Energy Shelf","kind":"cold","dl":"LONDON","line":"The coldest winter in a century locks Britain in ice. Coal cannot move; the lights go out.","unmade":"A mild winter on the North Sea. The coal moves; the grid holds.","worse":"The worst winter in three centuries. Britain's coal is under snow; the ports freeze.","date":"1947-01"},{"t":13,"dur":1,"region":"North American Plains","kind":"blizzard","dl":"OMAHA","line":"Blizzards bury the Plains. Operation Haylift drops feed to cattle from Air Force transports.","unmade":"A dry, open winter on the Plains. The cattle come through.","worse":"The Plains blizzards do not stop. Herds lost by the hundred thousand; Haylift cannot keep up.","date":"1949-01"},{"t":18,"dur":2,"region":"Eastern Australia","kind":"flood","dl":"SYDNEY","line":"The wettest year on record in New South Wales. The Hunter and the Macquarie over their banks for months.","unmade":"The rains that were forecast for New South Wales never arrive. A dry, ordinary year.","worse":"Floods in New South Wales beyond anything recorded. Maitland underwater a second time.","date":"1950-04"},{"t":19,"dur":2,"region":"South Asia","kind":"flood","dl":"SHILLONG","line":"The Brahmaputra, dammed by the earthquake's landslides, breaks through. Assam under water.","unmade":"The Brahmaputra stays low after the earthquake. Assam is spared.","worse":"The Brahmaputra floods on a scale no gauge can measure. Assam is an inland sea.","date":"1950-07"},{"t":23,"dur":1,"region":"North American Plains","kind":"flood","dl":"KANSAS CITY","line":"The Kansas and Missouri rivers over their levees. The Kansas City stockyards under fifteen feet of water.","unmade":"The Kansas River stays in its banks. A quiet July.","worse":"The Kansas and Missouri floods run for weeks. Both cities' stockyards are gone.","date":"1951-07"},{"t":29,"dur":1,"region":"North Sea Energy Shelf","kind":"flood","dl":"THE HAGUE","line":"The North Sea storm surge breaks the dikes of Zeeland and the Thames sea walls. 2,500 dead in a night.","unmade":"The February gale passes over the North Sea without a surge. The dikes hold. Nobody knows how close it came.","worse":"The North Sea surge overtops every dike from Zeeland to the Humber. The count stops at five thousand.","date":"1953-01"},{"t":33,"dur":4,"region":"North American Plains","kind":"drought","dl":"AMARILLO","line":"Third year of drought in Texas and the southern Plains. Worse than the Thirties, the old men say.","unmade":"The rains return to the southern Plains. The drought the almanacs feared breaks a year early.","worse":"The southern Plains drought deepens. Dust over Amarillo again, thirty years on.","date":"1954-01"}]}